<title>PHILIPPINES: PLDT jumps 2.67 pct, most active issue.</title>
<headline>PLDT jumps 2.67 pct, most active issue.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippine Long Distance Telephone Co gained 25 pesos, or 2.67 percent, at 960 pesos in early trade riding the general wave of buying following a long-awaited decision of the Central Bank to lower interest rates.</p>
<p>&quot;Most issues including PLDT are just reacting to the fact that there's not much bad news anymore at this point,&quot; said Helen Alvarez, research director at All Asia Securities.</p>
</text>
